Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: wine, 7zip, dosbox, qemu-user, desktop-file-utils
Suggests: darling, box64, winetricks, default-jre
Homepage: https://github.com/SoloB3n/UniOS
Description: run Linux, Windows and macOS programs from the same system
 UniOS recognises the format of every executable (ELF, PE, Mach-O, .app,
 .dmg, .pkg, .msi) and starts it with the right compatibility layer: native,
 Wine, Darling or DOSBox, with CPU translation when needed. It registers the
 formats with binfmt_misc and the desktop menu, applies per-program profiles
 and installs applications into the menu.
